## Frequently Asked Questions About Beaumont Lemon Law

## Does my vehicle qualify for a CA lemon law claim?

Vehicles under a manufacturer or dealer warranty may be eligible for a CA lemon law claim if the warranty was still valid when the defect was reported.

Warranty terms vary across manufacturers, with many providing a standard 3-year/36,000-mile warranty for new vehicles. It’s important to familiarize yourself with the specifics of your warranty before you start the lemon law process.

## What if my vehicle is older than 18 months or has more than 18,000 miles?

The 18-month / 18,000-mile window is a lemon-law presumption, not a requirement. It does not decide whether you have a good case. What matters is whether the defect first occurred during the original manufacturer warranty. This is not true.

You are entitled to pursue a claim under CA lemon law if the defect was reported during the warranty period. The 18-month / 18,000-mile window is a lemon-law presumption, not a requirement. It does not decide whether you have a good case. What matters is whether the defect first occurred during the original manufacturer warranty.

## Do I need an attorney for my Beaumont lemon law case?

While it’s not mandatory to hire an attorney for your lemon law case, going it alone can significantly reduce your chances of receiving fair compensation. Car manufacturers have strategies in place to avoid legal responsibility for selling defective vehicles.

A seasoned Beaumont lemon law attorney knows how to navigate these tactics, ensuring you get the best possible outcome. An attorney acts as your advocate, fighting for your rights and preventing delays by the manufacturer.

## What is the statute of limitations for filing a CA lemon law claim?

You have a four-year period from the date of the issue to file a lemon law claim in California. Starting the process sooner rather than later is advisable, as delays can complicate your case and pose safety risks. Continuing to use a defective vehicle is dangerous for both you and others on the road.

## What if I prefer a replacement vehicle to a buyback?

If you’re loyal to your car brand and understand that mistakes happen, you might opt for a replacement vehicle of the same model or equivalent value. However, it’s essential to remember that manufacturers are not legally required to offer a replacement and must agree to this option.

## What about cars bought in private sales?

California lemon law typically does not cover vehicles purchased through private sales, as these are often sold “as is.” However, if the vehicle’s warranty is still active and transferable to you, you may still be eligible for lemon law benefits.

## How long does a Beaumont lemon law claim take to resolve?

The duration of a lemon law claim can vary based on its specifics and complexity. Working with a skilled California lemon law attorney can streamline the process, aiming to resolve your claim as quickly as possible. Generally, claims are settled within a few weeks to a few months, depending on the case’s details.
